ns probe-1bvi-x

def env := {:prod {:db {:url "p-url" :port 5432}} :dev {:db {:url "d-url" :port 5433}}}
def kk := {:a {:k 1} :k 2}

;; 1b-vi-D-1: is `star-dup-key`'s sentence "If the key was lifted, dropping the `*`
;; does not help either: it re-nests the layer under the key the star was deleting"
;; true outside the one population it was written against (1b-iv)?
;; (1) both branches `*`, the deleted keys EQUAL — drop both `*`s / drop one
env{prod^.db* dev^.db*}
env{prod^.db dev^.db}
env{prod^.db dev^.db*}
;; (2) a LIFTED key colliding with a key another branch NAMES — drop the `*`
kk{a* k}
kk{a k}
;; (3) a MIXED block — drop the `*` / drop the `*-` (spelled by its ≡)
env{prod^.db* dev^.db*}
env{prod^.db dev^.db*}
env{prod^.db* dev.db}
;; (4) the generic remedy "select the flatten in its own block"
kk{a*}
kk{k}
